          header: "Simplifying the network configuration",
          value: "After several years of experience, I deliberately simplified the infrastructure because some of its components were no longer necessary. The dual-ISP setup worked well, but it was relatively expensive to maintain. What's more, it had come in handy only once over the course of several years. I also often found myself adding firewall rules to allow communication between subnets, which undermined the whole point of maintaining such a setup. These factors led me to simplify the network after moving. I gave up the VPS, the secondary ISP, and the managed switch, replacing the latter with a small, energy-efficient TP-Link switch mounted in the rack in a 3D-printed bracket.",
